WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.292
Once you define possible routes, limit the model to those allowed values.

00:00:05.292 --> 00:00:13.042
Suppose the valid routes are policy search, order lookup, policy and order, and answer directly.

00:00:13.042 --> 00:00:19.888
If the model returns something else, the application should reject it rather than guessing what the model meant.

00:00:20.478 --> 00:00:24.985
In Python, you can validate the returned string against a set.

00:00:24.985 --> 00:00:33.060
With typed structured output, you can define a literal or enum so the allowed choices are part of the schema.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:38.525
This converts open-ended model language into a finite state-machine decision.

00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:47.325
For example, if the model returns search everything, but that route is not allowed, the controller should not improvise.

00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:49.766
It should treat the output as invalid.

00:00:50.484 --> 00:00:55.815
Finite choices improve reliability, testability, and security.
